---
description: Project rules for meeting-manager-backend (all agents)
alwaysApply: true
---
Follow `AGENTS.md` in the repo root — it is the single source of rules (stack, structure, patterns, ownership, workflow).

Key points:
- Cursor owns the whole backend, including shared files and `docs/api-contract.md`.
- Contract changes go in a separate `contract: ...` PR; the frontend (Claude) depends on it.
- Use `AppError`, `parseBody/parseQuery/parseParams`, `deps.db`, `deps.now()`, `req.log`; ESM `.js` imports.
- Never log passwords, OTP codes, cookies, tokens, emails or bodies. No JWT.
- Never edit merged migrations; generate new ones with `npm run db:generate`.
- Done = typecheck + tests + build green; Conventional Commits in English; Codex reviews every PR.
